# The themed trails added in November 2026 (Ifan asked for many more trails, 12 November 2026).
# long.py puts these in front of its own four trails (newest first), and build.py makes trail-<id>.html for each.
#
# A stop is one of:
#   ("event", "English title exactly as in data.py")
#   ("person", slug) | ("place", id)
#   ("story", id) | ("story", id, dateEn, dateCy)      a long read; left out until it is on the site
#   ("legend", id) | ("legend", id, dateEn, dateCy)    a legend page
#   ("page", href, era, dateEn, dateCy, titleEn, titleCy, textEn, textCy)
# Keep each trail to 8 to 10 stops, in order of time. Keep the number of trails a multiple of 6 (18, 24 ...) so the
# grid on trails.html has no empty space at three columns or at two. Follow EDITORIAL.md: proud and true, Britons not
# Celts, kings are kings, Arthur in the words of Welsh tradition.

